      },
      "proposed_fix": "Replace `httpx.WSGITransport` with `httpx.WSGICarrier` in the HTTPX transports documentation."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "DD-10",
      "drift_kind": "name",
      "explanation": "The HTTPX custom transport example uses `httpx.Marks`, but HTTPX does not expose a `Mounts` class; mounted transports are configured with the client `mounts` mapping.",
      "doc_citation": {
        "path": "httpx/docs/advanced/transports.md",
        "start_line": 191,
        "end_line": 194,
        "quote": "mounts = {'http://': HTTPSRedirectTransport()}\nclient = httpx.Client(mounts=mounts)"
      },
      "code_citation": {
        "path": "httpx/httpx/_client.py",
        "start_line": 697,
        "end_line": 699,
        "quote": "self._mounts: dict[URLPattern, BaseTransport | None] = {\n            URLPattern(key): None\n            if proxy is None"
      },
      "proposed_fix": "Remove the nonexistent `httpx.Mounts` example or replace it with passing a `mounts` mapping to `httpx.Client`."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "DD-11",
      "drift_kind": "signature",
      "explanation": "The HTTPX custom transport example declares an old five-parameter `handle_request` method, but the current `BaseTransport.handle_request` method takes a single `Request` instance.",
      "doc_citation": {
        "path": "httpx/docs/advanced/transports.md",
        "start_line": 285,
        "end_line": 286,
        "quote": "def handle_request(self, method, url, headers, stream, extensions):\n        scheme, host, port, path = url"
      },
      "code_citation": {
        "path": "httpx/httpx/_transports/base.py",
        "start_line": 26,
        "end_line": 27,
        "quote": "def handle_request(self, request: Request) -> Response:\n        \"\"\""
      },
      "proposed_fix": "Update the custom transport example to implement `handle_request(self, request: httpx.Request) -> httpx.Response`."
    }
  ],
